[ti:Pretend]
[ar:Ash Stu]
[al:Ash Stu, Vol. I]
[re:aligned with Demucs vocal separation + MMS forced alignment; edit timestamps by hand if a line is off]
[00:12.88]I want so bad to sort my thoughts
[00:17.20]But don't know where to start
[00:19.94]I'll never get the words across
[00:23.94]To mean what's in my heart
[00:26.80]I'll reach the cusp of clarity
[00:29.85]Then lose my grip so soon
[00:32.72]My brain and mouth need parity
[00:36.86]I can't bring them in tune
[00:39.70]So many pictures in my mind
[00:44.24]And I can't seem to free them
[00:47.91]I look for words, but never find
[00:50.33]The accurate descriptions
[00:54.77]I want so bad to write a song
[00:58.22]That opens up my head
[01:01.18]It hurts to always get it wrong
[01:04.52]When so much could be said
[01:21.32]I dream I wrote you "Anna-Lee"
[01:27.73]By Edgar Allan Poe
[01:34.27]He phrases thoughts so beautifully
[01:39.46]With lovely structured flow
[01:46.54]If I could write one-tenth as wise
[01:50.75]As he, you'd understand
[01:54.01]The colors that flash through my eyes
[01:58.28]With each touch of your hands
[02:00.92]I wish I wrote "Shall I Compare
[02:03.96]Thee to a Summer's Day"
[02:07.21]Like Shakespeare spoke, lost in the stare
[02:10.69]Of Agnes Hathaway
[02:13.71]If I could write one tenth as clear
[02:16.68]As he, you might perceive
[02:19.30]The orchestra that's in my ear
[02:23.52]When listening to you breathe
[02:24.90]But I'm giving you everything that I got
[02:36.64]I know it isn't all that you deserve
[02:43.52]The feeling is there but when I talk my tongue gets caught
[02:50.85]I'm always tryna' chase down every word
[02:55.28]So just pretend that I'm a better poet
[03:03.98]Lord knows I'd love to be
[03:07.88]Then maybe you will see
[03:33.69]Me, as I see you
